Add public reset() method to DirectiveHashCollection.

DirectiveHashCollection accumulates CSP hash values for inline and
static assets. Under long-running runtimes the same instance
persists, causing unbounded CSP header growth and information
disclosure as hash values from previous responses leak.

Add a public reset() method to clear all accumulated hash values
back to the initial empty state.

--- a/Classes/Security/ContentSecurityPolicy/DirectiveHashCollection.php
+++ b/Classes/Security/ContentSecurityPolicy/DirectiveHashCollection.php
@@ -50,6 +50,22 @@
     public function __construct(private readonly ResourceHashCollection $resourceHashCollection) {}
 
     /**
+     * Clears all accumulated hash values back to the initial empty state.
+     *
+     * Useful for long-running PHP runtimes where this shared service
+     * persists across requests and hash values must not leak.
+     */
+    public function reset(): void
+    {
+        $this->hashValues = [
+            'inline' => [],
+            'resource' => [],
+            'uri' => [],
+            'generic' => [],
+        ];
+    }
+
+    /**
      * Computes a SHA-256 hash of the given inline content and stores it for the directive.
      */
     public function addInlineHash(Directive $directive, string $content): void
